// quest-consent-dictionary.js
// Source: Brent, Aug 2026 -- CR: add Spanish-language consent text (Rachel A.
// Hardin / Quest, 8/20/2026 email + "Consents for Zingtree 2.xlsx") and
// consolidate the old "Cigna Consent English 2024" / "Cigna Consent Spanish
// 2020" split into a single "cigna_consent" entry driven by the new
// Preferred Language field at intake (node 1) instead of a duplicate
// dropdown option.
// Purpose: company_score -> consent text (English + Spanish where Quest has
// supplied a professional translation), display client name, client ID.
// Mirrors clientData in node 6 and inverseClientData in the User Consent
// tree's node 4 -- keep all three in sync when clients/consents are added.
//
// NOTE (known, out of scope for this CR): the dictionary key
// "solutions_program_authorization_for_release_of_health_screening_results__rock_and_roll_hall_of_fame"
// does not match either of the two original dropdown score values
// ("solutions_program_authorization_for_release_of_health_screening_results"
// and "rock_and_roll_hall_of_fame") -- both of those menu options have
// resolved to blank consent text since before this CR. Left unchanged here;
// flagged in the requirements doc for a separate fix.
//
// Rachel Hardin's 8/20/2026 spreadsheet also introduced a ~400-client roster
// mapped to just 12 shared consent templates -- Brent scoped THIS CR to the
// original 18 clients only; the larger roster is not wired into the dropdown.

// Update, Aug 31 2026 -- CR (Marcus Torres Slack DM 8/31 + Quest emails):
// (1) healthyquest_bfw_hipaa_authorization_08292025 consent_en refreshed to the
//     approved 2026 BFW HIPAA Authorization language (Mike Marks email 8/29/2026,
//     "Quest - BFW - HIPAA Authorization 2026.pdf"): claims administrators now
//     include Priority Health and Kaiser; "smoking cessation" -> "nicotine
//     cessation"; minor formatting fixes. consent_es NOT yet refreshed -- Quest
//     has not supplied an updated Spanish translation; Spanish renders the prior
//     revision until they do. The optional research consent language for Healthy
//     Quest is still awaiting Quest approval -- not touched here.
// (2) Added parker_hannifin_2026_myguide (Rachel A. Hardin email 8/21/2026,
//     "Parker Hannifin Disclosure-Attestation.docx", program "2026 MyGuide"):
//     Unum disclosure attestation, English only, client ID pending from Quest.
var dictionary = {
  "autonation_consent": { "consent_en": "By registering for and participating in the AutoNation MSRP biometric screening program, I understand and agree that my individual test results will be shared with certain contracted third parties including, but not limited to, insurance carriers and AutoNation Benefit Plan (“Plan”) consultants. By clicking “I Agree” below, I am providing consent to the secure and confidential transfer of my test results to contracted third parties for the purpose of enhancing patient care services, assisting with Plan communications and/or Plan administration and management and processing my screening results and determining which healthy incentive credits apply to me. In order to be eligible for healthy incentive credits, I must fully participate in all required screening components and testing procedures. AutoNation will NOT receive individual biometric screening results. If I do not pass 3 of 5 MSRP biometric lab risk factors I acknowledge and agree The Benefit Connection will notify me via my preferred email address (if I established one) or my AutoNation email address registered on The Benefit Connection website, of the alternate methods for earning the healthy incentive credits. If I am the spouse of an AutoNation employee I am acknowledging and consenting that the email for me will be sent to my preferred email (if applicable) or my spouse’s AutoNation email address registered on The Benefit Connection website. The actual results of my MSRP biometric screening will not be reported to The Benefit Connection, simply an indicator noting if I am eligible for the healthy credits based on my screening.", "consent_es": "Al inscribirme y participar en el programa de evaluación biométrica MSRP de AutoNation, comprendo y acepto que los resultados individuales de mis pruebas se compartirán con determinados terceros contratados, incluidas, entre otras, las compañías de seguros y los consultores del Plan de Beneficios de AutoNation (el "Plan"). Al hacer clic en "Acepto" más abajo, doy mi consentimiento para la transferencia segura y confidencial de los resultados de mis pruebas a terceros contratados con el fin de mejorar los servicios de atención al paciente, facilitar las comunicaciones y/o la administración y gestión del Plan, procesar los resultados de mi evaluación y determinar qué créditos de incentivo por hábitos saludables me corresponden. Para poder optar a los créditos de incentivo por hábitos saludables, debo participar plenamente en todos los componentes de la evaluación y en los procedimientos de prueba requeridos. AutoNation NO recibirá los resultados individuales de la evaluación biométrica. Si no supero 3 de los 5 factores de riesgo de laboratorio de la evaluación biométrica MSRP, reconozco y acepto que The Benefit Connection me notificará —a través de mi dirección de correo electrónico preferida (si la he establecido) o de mi dirección de correo electrónico de AutoNation registrada en el sitio web de The Benefit Connection— sobre los métodos alternativos para obtener los créditos de incentivo por hábitos saludables. Si soy cónyuge de un empleado de AutoNation, reconozco y acepto que las notificaciones por correo electrónico se enviarán a mi dirección preferida (si corresponde) o a la dirección de correo electrónico de AutoNation de mi cónyuge registrada en el sitio web de The Benefit Connection. Los resultados detallados de mi evaluación biométrica MSRP no se comunicarán a The Benefit Connection; únicamente se informará de un indicador que señale si reúno los requisitos para obtener los créditos por hábitos saludables en función de dicha evaluación.", "client name": "AutoNation", "client ID": "10035" },
  "honeywell_international_inc": { "consent_en": "Honeywell’s wellness program (the Program) is voluntary and available to all employees.  By completing a biometric screening, you authorize the results to be sent from Quest Diagnostics to applicable service providers associated with the Program (Service Providers) including Cigna or Castlight Health, for health navigation services, and Merative, a healthcare analytics solution provider. We are required by law to maintain the privacy and security of your personally identifiable health information. Although the Program and Honeywell may use aggregate information collected to design a program based on identified health risks in the workplace, neither the Program nor the Service Providers will disclose any of your personal information either publicly or to Honeywell, except as necessary to respond to a request from you for a reasonable accommodation needed to participate in the Program, or as expressly permitted by law. Medical information that personally identifies you that is provided in connection with the Program will not be provided to your supervisors or managers and may never be used to make decisions regarding your employment.", "consent_es": "El programa de bienestar de Honeywell (el Programa) es voluntario y está disponible para todos los empleados. Al completar una evaluación biométrica, usted autoriza que los resultados se envíen desde Quest Diagnostics a los proveedores de servicios pertinentes asociados con el Programa (Proveedores de Servicios) —incluidos Cigna o Castlight Health, para servicios de orientación en salud, y Merative, un proveedor de soluciones de análisis de datos de salud—. Por ley, estamos obligados a mantener la privacidad y seguridad de su información de salud de identificación personal. Si bien el Programa y Honeywell pueden utilizar la información agregada recopilada para diseñar un programa basado en los riesgos de salud identificados en el lugar de trabajo, ni el Programa ni los Proveedores de Servicios divulgarán su información personal, ya sea públicamente o a Honeywell, salvo cuando sea necesario para atender una solicitud suya de adaptación razonable para participar en el Programa, o según lo permita expresamente la ley. La información médica que le identifique personalmente y que se proporcione en relación con el Programa no se facilitará a sus supervisores o gerentes, y bajo ninguna circunstancia se utilizará para tomar decisiones relativas a su empleo.", "client name": "Honeywell", "client ID": "10430" },
  "bcbs_of_alabama_custom_consent": { "consent_en": "I understand that this screening service is offered for my benefit and information. Screening tests are not meant to replace the care of my personal physician. I acknowledge that I may receive results that are considered “out of range” as well as an explanation for these results. However, I also understand that screening tests can give false positive or negative results for a variety of reasons. I acknowledge that my physician is best able to interpret the results of these tests based on his/her understanding of my medical history. I also acknowledge that I have received a copy of my group health plan's Notice of Privacy Practices and understand such Notice provides an explanation of the ways that my individual health information may be stored, used or disclosed by my group health plan and those acting on behalf of my group health plan (for example group health plan and its business associates WebMD, and Quest Diagnostics), and of my rights with respect to my health information. This means, among other things, that my group health plan may use and disclose my wellness screening results for the group health plan's healthcare operations. I have been provided the opportunity to discuss concerns I may have regarding the privacy of my health information. I understand that Quest Diagnostics may share my wellness screening results with group health plan (and its business associate WebMD) if I am, or become, a registered user of the WebMD internet tools provided by group health plan for use by my group health plan's members.

I release and discharge my group health plan, Quest Diagnostics, WebMD and their shareholders, parent, subsidiaries, officers, directors, employees, franchisees, licensees, vendors used to conduct lab analyses, subcontractors and, respective affiliates, and the program sponsors, including, without limitation, WebMD and their agents, including the owners/operators of this facility and its parent, subsidiaries, officers, directors and employees (collectively, the “Released Parties”), from any and all claims or causes of action, on account of injury to me which may result from my participation in this screening (including a failure of the screening to detect any particular health problem), except for such claims or causes of action on account of injury to me resulting from the sole negligent acts or omissions, or willful misconduct, of the Released Parties. This release shall be binding upon my heirs, assigns, executors, administrators and representatives.

Quest Diagnostics and WebMD are independent companies that provide worksite wellness services to group health plan customers.", "consent_es": "Entiendo que este servicio de pruebas de detección se ofrece para mi beneficio e información. Las pruebas de detección no pretenden sustituir la atención de mi médico personal. Reconozco que puedo recibir resultados considerados "fuera de rango", así como una explicación de dichos resultados. Sin embargo, también entiendo que las pruebas de detección pueden arrojar resultados falsos positivos o negativos por diversas razones. Reconozco que mi médico es quien mejor puede interpretar los resultados de estas pruebas basándose en su conocimiento de mi historial médico. Asimismo, reconozco haber recibido una copia del Aviso de Prácticas de Privacidad de mi plan de salud grupal y entiendo que dicho aviso explica cómo mi plan de salud grupal y aquellos que actúan en su nombre (por ejemplo, el plan de salud grupal y sus socios comerciales WebMD y Quest Diagnostics) pueden almacenar, utilizar o divulgar mi información de salud individual, así como mis derechos con respecto a dicha información. Esto significa, entre otras cosas, que mi plan de salud grupal puede utilizar y divulgar los resultados de mis pruebas de detección de bienestar para las operaciones de atención médica del propio plan. Se me ha dado la oportunidad de hablar sobre cualquier inquietud que pudiera tener respecto a la privacidad de mi información de salud. Entiendo que Quest Diagnostics puede compartir los resultados de mis pruebas de detección de bienestar con el plan de salud grupal (y su socio comercial WebMD) si soy, o llego a ser, usuario registrado de las herramientas de Internet de WebMD proporcionadas por el plan de salud grupal para uso de sus miembros.

Eximo y libero de responsabilidad a mi plan de salud grupal, a Quest Diagnostics, a WebMD y a sus accionistas, empresa matriz, filiales, funcionarios, directores, empleados, franquiciados, licenciatarios, proveedores utilizados para realizar análisis de laboratorio, subcontratistas y sus respectivas afiliadas, así como a los patrocinadores del programa —incluidos, entre otros, WebMD y sus agentes, así como los propietarios/operadores de estas instalaciones y su empresa matriz, filiales, funcionarios, directores y empleados (colectivamente, las "Partes Eximidas de Responsabilidad")— de cualquier reclamación o causa de acción derivada de lesiones que yo pudiera sufrir como resultado de mi participación en esta prueba de detección (incluida la falta de detección de algún problema de salud específico), excepto aquellas reclamaciones o causas de acción por lesiones resultantes de actos u omisiones de negligencia exclusiva o de mala conducta intencional por parte de las Partes Eximidas de Responsabilidad. Esta exención de responsabilidad será vinculante para mis herederos, cesionarios, albaceas, administradores y representantes. Quest Diagnostics y WebMD son empresas independientes que ofrecen servicios de bienestar en el lugar de trabajo a clientes de planes de salud grupales.", "client name": "BCBS of Alabama", "client ID": "20248" },
  "partners_for_health_consent": { "consent_en": "I consent to participate in

Active Health Management's Health Risk Screening and Support Program (the "Program"), which may include providing biometric measurements such as weight and blood pressure, disclosing laboratory results from a recent blood test with my personal physician, and/or completing an on-line or written Health Risk Assessment.

I understand that my participation in the Program is voluntary and that I am not required to participate as a condition of employment or of enrollment in my health plan.

I understand and consent to my personal physician providing to Quest on behalf of ActiveHealth Management results from a blood draw and laboratory analysis performed by my physician within the past twelve (12) months for the tests listed below.

I agree to execute any authorization form required by my physician prior to disclosing my results to ActiveHealth Management.

Such results will include lipids (cholesterol and components) and blood glucose measurements in addition to blood pressure, height, weight and waist.

I consent to Quest providing me with a report (either on-line or in writing) of my Program results and, if applicable, periodically providing me with follow-up educational materials and information relevant to my Program results.

The laboratory results reflected in my report are for informational purposes only and are NOT a medical diagnosis.

I understand that the Program is sponsored by my employer or benefits provider.

If an incentive is implemented as part of the Program, I consent to Quest informing my Sponsor only whether or not I qualify for such incentive based upon my participation in the Program.

I understand that if I do not elect to provide such consent, I may not qualify for such incentive.

I understand that my individual health data will be used by ActiveHealth Management and will be treated as confidential in accordance with the Health Insurance Portability and Accountability Act of 1996 (HIPAA).

Individual health information will be shared between my physician or care provider and Quest, however individual information will not be shared with my employer.

I understand that ActiveHealth Management will not disclose my individual health information to my employer.

Aggregated data (i.e., data with no individual identifiers) on all participants, however, may be shared with employer.

I understand that my employer or benefits provider may from time to time offer enrollees other health and wellness services and programs (collectively, "Other Health/Wellness Programs"), such as employee assistance and/or disease management programs.

I consent to the disclosure by ActiveHealth Management of my wellness screening results and/or other personal health information that identifies me to ActiveHealth Management' other Health/Wellness Programs so that they may contact me for the purpose of addressing my particular health/wellness needs.

I understand that ActiveHealth Management and/or my employer or benefits provider will require such Other Health/Wellness Program providers to agree to maintain the confidentiality of any wellness screening results and/or other personal health information provided to them by ActiveHealth Management in accordance with the applicable regulations under HIPAA.

I understand that if I do not want ActiveHealth Management to disclose my wellness screening results and/or other personal health information to Other Health/Wellness Program providers sponsored by my employer or benefits provider, I must notify ActiveHealth Management in writing at:
ActiveHealth Management, PO Box 221138, Chantilly VA 20153-1138 Attn:
Screening Operations.

I understand that this consent will remain in effect for as long as I participate in the Program, and that I am entitled to a copy of this consent.

I may revoke this consent at any time by notifying ActiveHealth Management in writing, to the extent ActiveHealth Management has not already relied on this consent.", "client name": "State of Tennessee", "client ID": "29820" },
  "solutions_program_authorization_for_release_of_health_screening_results__rock_and_roll_hall_of_fame": { "consent_en": "The Genetic Information Nondiscrimination Act of 2008 (GINA) prohibits employers and other entities covered by GINA Title II from requesting or requiring genetic information of an individual or family member of the individual, except as specifically allowed by this law.

To comply with this law, we are asking that you not provide any genetic information when responding to this request for medical information.
'Genetic information' as defined by GINA, includes an individual's family medical history, the results of an individual's or family member's genetic tests, the fact that an individual or an individual's family member sought or received genetic services, and genetic information of a fetus carried by an individual or an individual's family member or an embryo lawfully held by an individual or family member receiving assistive reproductive services.

I authorize Medical Mutual of Ohio and its subsidiaries and affiliated companies (collectively, "Medical Mutual") to release to Rock & Roll Hall of Fame the number of health factors I met gathered from my health screening for the purposes of coordinating with the Rock & Roll Hall of Fame or the receipt of wellness benefits.

No specific results, including the specific factors met or not met nor the specific measures or test results will be shared with my employer.

I understand information used or disclosed pursuant to this Authorization may be subject to re-disclosure by the Rock & Roll Hall of Fame and may no longer be protected by Federal or State privacy laws.

**`I understand this authorization is voluntary, my participation in the wellness program is voluntary, and I will not be penalized if I choose not to participate in the Outcomes-Based Wellness Program.`**
I may revoke this authorization at any time by delivering such revocation in writing to Medical Mutual at:
Wellness Team;
MZ:
01-5B-7500;
Medical Mutual 2060 East 9th Street;
Cleveland, Ohio 44115.

I further understand Medical Mutual may not condition treatment, payment, enrollment or eligibility for benefits on my signing this Authorization.

I hereby release Medical Mutual from all legal responsibilities or liabilities that may arise from any use or disclosure of information made pursuant to this Authorization, and further understand and agree that any use of my individual health information by the Rock & Roll Hall of Fame is independent from the health plan programs and services provided by Medical Mutual.

This Authorization shall remain in effect as long as I participate in my employer's wellness program, unless revoked earlier by me in writing.

I certify that I have read, understand and agree to this Authorization.", "client name": "Rock and Roll Hall of Fame", "client ID": "33903" },
  "sharecare_1272020": { "consent_en": "Wellness Notice and Consent

I agree to participate in Sharecare’s Health Risk Screening and Support Program (the “Program”). I understand the Program is offered by my health plan or my employer as the sponsor of my health plan (“Sponsor”). I understand that completion of this biometric screening or vaccination is voluntary. If I choose not to participate or do not give my permission by signing this authorization form and completing this screening, I understand that I may not be able to receive Program incentives (if offered). The biometric screening data includes data which may be considered genetic information. I further understand that if choose to participate in the biometric screening or vaccination, any health and genetic information obtained in the screening will not be sold, exchanged, transferred, or otherwise disclosed except to the extent permitted by law to carry out specific activities related to the wellness program.
The Program may include the administration of a vaccination or collecting blood, by fingerstick or through a vein (venipuncture), for testing, identifying your unique behaviors (biometric measurements), completing a health risk or well-being assessment or other wellness activities. The blood test include but are not limited to: Total Cholesterol, High Density Lipoprotein (HDL), Low Density Lipoprotein (LDL), Triglycerides, Glucose, Cotinine, Gamma-Glutamyl Transferase (GGT), Albumin, Bilirubin, Blood Urea Nitrogen (BUN), Calcium, Globulin, Lactic Dehydrogenase, Phosphate/Alkaline, Protein, Serum Creatinine, Transferase Alanine, Transferase Asparte, Uric Acid, Very low density lipoprotein. This collection may also include recording of biometric measurements of Height, Weight, Waist Circumference, Blood Pressure and calculated Body Mass Index (BMI).
If a blood sample is included in the Program (by fingerstick or venipuncture), I give my permission to have my blood drawn and agree that I have been made aware of the possible related risks. These risks may include infection, soreness and bruising. I understand that more risks may occur and the information I have been given is enough for me to give my permission for the collection of my blood sample.
I also give my permission for my blood sample to be studied, in a laboratory (working with Sharecare) or at the onsite screening, and if a laboratory is used, it may give my results to Sharecare. I release Sharecare, the laboratory and other companies or people working with the Program from any and all liability coming from Program screenings, the collection of my blood sample, the laboratory study of my blood sample, if needed, and the report of the study of my blood sample.
I understand that all information and comments I receive through the Program, including any test results, are early pieces of information gathered through the brief review that has taken place, and are NOT a medical diagnosis or opinion. Participation in the Program does not take the place of professional medical advice. I must call or visit my doctor to talk about any questions I have about my test, screening, or lab results or to get medical opinions.
I understand and give my permission for Sharecare to use and share my personal health information as allowed by law, including the Health Insurance Portability and Accountability Act of 1996 (HIPAA). My personal health information may have my name, participation status, screening results, vaccination date and other information. I also give my permission for Sharecare to share my information in order to operate the Program, and to other programs offered by my Sponsor to provide wellness services to me.
Sharecare may depend on my permission for as long as I participate in the Program. I may revoke this permission at any time by writing to Sharecare. The removal of my permission does not apply to any use or sharing of my information by Sharecare before I write to them. Any notice to Sharecare should be mailed to Sharecare, 255 East Paces Ferry Road  Northeast,  Suite 700, Atlanta, GA 30305, Attention: Privacy Office", "consent_es": "Aviso y consentimiento sobre bienestar

Acepto participar en el Programa de Apoyo y Evaluación de Riesgos para la Salud de Sharecare (el "Programa"). Entiendo que el Programa es ofrecido por mi plan de salud o por mi empleador en calidad de patrocinador de dicho plan ("Patrocinador"). Entiendo que completar esta evaluación biométrica o recibir la vacunación es voluntario. Si decido no participar o no doy mi permiso firmando este formulario de autorización y completando la evaluación, entiendo que es posible que no pueda recibir los incentivos del Programa (si se ofrecen). Los datos de la evaluación biométrica incluyen información que podría considerarse información genética. Asimismo, entiendo que, si decido participar en la evaluación biométrica o en la vacunación, cualquier información de salud o genética obtenida durante la evaluación no se venderá, intercambiará, transferirá ni divulgará de otro modo, salvo en la medida permitida por la ley para llevar a cabo actividades específicas relacionadas con el programa de bienestar.
El Programa puede incluir la administración de una vacuna o la extracción de sangre —mediante punción en el dedo o a través de una vena (venopunción)— para realizar análisis, identificar características únicas (mediciones biométricas), completar una evaluación de riesgos para la salud o de bienestar, u otras actividades relacionadas con el bienestar. Los análisis de sangre incluyen, entre otros: colesterol total, lipoproteína de alta densidad (HDL), lipoproteína de baja densidad (LDL), triglicéridos, glucosa, cotinina, gamma-glutamil transferasa (GGT), albúmina, bilirrubina, nitrógeno ureico en sangre (BUN), calcio, globulina, lactato deshidrogenasa, fosfato/fosfatasa alcalina, proteínas, creatinina sérica, alanina aminotransferasa (ALT), aspartato aminotransferasa (AST), ácido úrico y lipoproteína de muy baja densidad (VLDL). Esta recopilación también puede incluir el registro de mediciones biométricas como estatura, peso, circunferencia de la cintura, presión arterial y el cálculo del índice de masa corporal (IMC).
Si el Programa incluye una muestra de sangre (mediante punción en el dedo o venopunción), doy mi permiso para que se me extraiga sangre y reconozco haber sido informado sobre los posibles riesgos asociados. Estos riesgos pueden incluir infección, dolor y hematomas. Entiendo que pueden surgir otros riesgos y que la información que he recibido es suficiente para otorgar mi permiso para la extracción de la muestra de sangre. También autorizo ​​que mi muestra de sangre sea analizada, ya sea en un laboratorio (que colabore con Sharecare) o durante la evaluación presencial; en caso de utilizarse un laboratorio, este podrá comunicar mis resultados a Sharecare. Eximo a Sharecare, al laboratorio y a cualquier otra empresa o persona que colabore con el Programa de toda responsabilidad derivada de las evaluaciones del Programa, la toma de mi muestra de sangre, el análisis de dicha muestra en el laboratorio (si fuera necesario) y el informe de los resultados de dicho análisis.
Entiendo que toda la información y los comentarios que reciba a través del Programa, incluidos los resultados de las pruebas, constituyen información preliminar obtenida mediante la breve evaluación realizada y NO representan un diagnóstico ni una opinión médica. La participación en el Programa no sustituye el asesoramiento médico profesional. Debo consultar a mi médico para hablar sobre cualquier duda que tenga respecto a las pruebas, la evaluación o los resultados de laboratorio, o bien para obtener opiniones médicas.
Entiendo y autorizo ​​a Sharecare a utilizar y compartir mi información personal de salud conforme a lo permitido por la ley, incluida la Ley de Portabilidad y Responsabilidad del Seguro Médico de 1996 (HIPAA). Mi información personal de salud puede incluir mi nombre, estado de participación, resultados de la evaluación, fecha de vacunación y otros datos. Asimismo, autorizo ​​a Sharecare a compartir mi información para la gestión del Programa y con otros programas ofrecidos por mi Patrocinador con el fin de prestarme servicios de bienestar.
Sharecare podrá basarse en mi autorización durante todo el tiempo que participe en el Programa. Puedo revocar esta autorización en cualquier momento mediante una notificación por escrito a Sharecare. La revocación de mi autorización no afectará el uso ni la divulgación de mi información realizados por Sharecare antes de dicha notificación. Cualquier notificación dirigida a Sharecare deberá enviarse por correo a: Sharecare, 255 East Paces Ferry Road Northeast, Suite 700, Atlanta, GA 30305; a la atención de: Privacy Office (Oficina de Privacidad).", "client name": "Sharecare", "client ID": "14503" },
  "shbp_2020": { "consent_en": "Wellness Notice and Consent

I agree to participate in Sharecare's Health Risk Screening and Support Program (the "Program").

I understand the Program is administered by Sharecare on behalf of the State Health Benefit Plan ("Sponsor").

I understand that completion of this biometric screening is voluntary.

If I choose not to participate or do not give my permission by signing this authorization form and completing this screening, I understand that I may not be able to receive the Program incentives (if offered).

The biometric screening data includes data which may be considered genetic information.

I further understand that if I choose to participate in the screening, any health and genetic information obtained in the screening will not be sold, exchanged, transferred, or otherwise disclosed except to the extent permitted by law to carry out specific activities related to the wellness program.

I understand that the Program may include collecting blood, by fingerstick or through a vein (venipuncture), for testing, identifying my unique behaviors (biometric measurements), completing a health risk or well-being assessment or other wellness activities.

The blood tests include but are not limited to:
Total Cholesterol, High Density Lipoprotein (HDL), Low Density Lipoprotein (LDL), Triglycerides, Glucose, and HbA1c.

This collection may also include recording of biometric measurements of height, weight, waist circumference, blood pressure and calculated Body Mass Index (BMI).

If a blood sample is included in the Program (by fingerstick or venipuncture), I give my permission to have my blood drawn and agree that I have been made aware of the possible related risks.

These risks may include infection, soreness and bruising.

I understand that more risks may occur and the information I have been given is enough for me to give my permission for the collection of my blood sample.

I also give my permission for my blood sample to be studied, in a laboratory (working with Sharecare) or at the onsite screening, and if a laboratory is used, it may give my results to Sharecare.

I release Sharecare, the laboratory and other companies or people working with the Program from any and all liability coming from the Program screenings, the collection of my blood sample, the laboratory study of my blood sample, if needed, and the report of the study of my blood sample.

I understand that all information and comments I receive through the Program, including any test results, are based on the brief review that has taken place, and are NOT a medical diagnosis or opinion.

Participation in the Program does not take the place of professional medical advice.

I must call or visit my doctor to talk about any questions I have about my test, screening, or lab results or to get medical opinions.

I understand and give my permission for Sharecare to use and share my personal health information as allowed by law, including the Health Insurance Portability and Accountability Act of 1996 (HIPAA).

My personal health information may have my name, participation status, screening results and other information.

I also give my permission for Sharecare to share my information with my Sponsor or medical claims administrator to operate the Program and with other programs offered by my Sponsor to provide wellness services to me.

I may revoke this permission at any time by writing to Sharecare.

The revocation of my permission does not apply to any use or sharing of my information by Sharecare before I write to them.

Any notice to Sharecare should be mailed to Sharecare, 701 Cool Springs Blvd., Franklin, TN 37067, Attn:
Privacy Officer.", "client name": "State of Georgia", "client ID": "30339" },
