  "healthyquest_bfw_hipaa_authorization_08292025": { "consent_en": "Blueprint for Wellness HIPAA Authorization 
Quest Diagnostics Clinical Laboratories, Inc. (Sponsor) sponsors the Group Welfare Plan of Quest 
Diagnostics (the Welfare Plan) which includes a variety of employee assistance programs.  One such 
program is the Blueprint for Wellness health screening and related wellness services (the Program).  
The Program includes: a clinical set of laboratory tests and measurements; a health risk assessment; 
and wellness services for qualifying participants.  The Program is administered by the Welfare Plan and 
Quest Diagnostics Health & Wellness LLC (Workforce Health Solutions), which offers employer health 
screening events and employment drug testing solutions.  
The clinical laboratory tests and measurements include, by way of example, blood testing for cotinine 
and other indicators of health risk/chronic conditions such as metabolic syndrome, diabetes, heart 
disease, etc.  Quest Diagnostics Incorporated and its affiliated CLIA clinical testing laboratories (the 
Quest Labs) conduct the testing and clinical measurements that are part of the Program.  
Workforce Health Solutions arranges for the services provided by the ordering healthcare provider 
(SteadyMD) and Quest Labs, administers the health risk assessment, and determines who meets the 
eligibility requirements, as determined by the Welfare Plan, for wellness services offered as part of the 
Program.  The Welfare Plan contracts with claims administrators (e.g., Aetna, UnitedHealthcare, 
University of Pittsburgh Medical Center Health Plan, Priority Health, Kaiser), health care providers, and providers of wellness 
services such as condition management, health coaching, nicotine cessation, and incentive programs, 
to provide the administration and wellness services that are part of the Program (Wellness Service 
Providers).  Some of the Wellness Service Providers may be subsidiaries or affiliates of Quest 
Diagnostics Incorporated.  
As part of the Program, the Welfare Plan will receive the results of and information concerning your 
cotinine blood test and metabolic syndrome testing and measurements for the purposes of 
determining whether you qualify for an incentive or reward under the Welfare Plan (specifically, a 
reduction in bi-weekly medical contribution for medical plan enrollees (Incentives)).  
The Welfare Plan is committed to helping you achieve your best health. Rewards for participating in 
the Program are available to all employees enrolled in a Quest medical plan. If you think you might be 
unable to meet a standard for a reward under the Program, you might qualify for an opportunity to 
earn the same reward by different means. A reasonable alternative program may be available to you, 
or you may submit a physician affidavit form confirming that you are under the care of a doctor. 
Contact the Quest Diagnostics HR Service Center at (855) 411-8511 or visit the Blueprint for Wellness 
page at QuestHRSC.com to learn more. 
The Program is fully voluntary and offered at no cost to you. As part of the Program, Quest Labs, 
Workforce Health Solutions, and the Welfare Plan may need to share some of your personal health 
information (also known as your protected health information or PHI) with the Recipients for the 
Purposes described below.  
Authorization to Share PHI 
I give my permission and authorize Quest Labs, Workforce Health Solutions, and the Welfare Plan to 
collect, use and disclose my Blueprint for Wellness PHI to the groups and individuals named as 
Recipients for the Purposes as described below in this Authorization.  
The Purpose of this authorization is to share your PHI with the Recipients (defined below) to arrange 
for the wellness services that you are eligible for through the Program.   
PHI means your personal information (e.g., name, address, age, gender, and other personal 
information) and any and all information related the clinical testing and measurements, and the health 
risk assessment as part of the Program, including but not limited to, information to book 
appointment(s), answers provided on your health questionnaire, your test results, your Metabolic 
Syndrome (MetS) Rewards score and your Blueprint for Wellness Health Quotient score. 
Recipients means the following groups and individuals, who will receive or have access to your PHI: 
Quest Diagnostics Incorporated personnel who share Program participant eligibility lists with Wellness 
Service Providers; Quest Diagnostics Incorporated personnel who are involved in administering the 
Incentives for qualifying participants; Wellness Service Providers.  
To the extent any Recipients are not HIPAA covered entities or business associates, once a Recipient 
has your PHI, it may no longer be protected under federal privacy law and it could be re-disclosed or 
re-shared to others.   
This Authorization takes effect when I sign it; my authorization will expire upon revocation or such 
shorter period (if any) required by state law.   
